1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:06,700
GTA 6 is finally out, and even a PS5 Pro can't run it at 60 frames a second.

2
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:18,160
Digital Foundry measured a 30 frame cap on both PlayStation 5 models, around 1440p, with no performance mode.

3
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:20,939
The graphics chip isn't the problem.

4
00:00:21,219 --> 00:00:27,390
Every pedestrian and car runs on the processor: eight Zen 2 cores from 2020.

5
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:34,876
The PS5 Pro's GPU is much bigger, but its processor is only about ten percent faster.

6
00:00:35,156 --> 00:00:37,330
So it just holds 30 more steadily.

7
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,551
PC isn't announced.

8
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:48,690
One report says early 2027, and Digital Foundry warns even double the console's speed may miss 60 in crowds.

9
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,095
So what will your PC need?

10
00:00:51,375 --> 00:00:52,801
Full breakdown Monday.

11
00:00:53,081 --> 00:00:55,877
Share this, subscribe, and comment your questions.

